    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0047" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg33"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)Colombia/582: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-16T21:00:00-04:00">March 16, 1943—9 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>327. Embassy’s telegram 452, March 13, 7 p.m. In view of the desire of the Acting
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs, the Department withdraws its objection to the
                    inclusion of numbered paragraph 10 in the draft text of the proposed note.</p>
                <p>Accordingly, you may proceed with the drafting of the note with the inclusion of
                    paragraph 10. When you are satisfied that the revised draft embodies the
                    amendment and clarification of numbered paragraphs 3 and 5, as suggested in
                    Department’s telegram 292 of March 10, you may proceed with the exchange of
                        notes.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d37-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d37-f1" n="65" xml:id="d37-f1-content">
                <p>The notes were signed and exchanged on March 29, 1943. For texts, see Executive
                    Agreement Series No. 442, or 58 Stat. (pt. 2) 1546.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
